  "@type": "Process",
  "critical": false,
  "description": "Design of solid propellant grain geometry to tailor the thrust-time profile. Star, cylindrical (core-burning), and finocyl (finned-cylinder) cross-sections set the burning surface area evolution, producing progressive (rising thrust), regressive (falling thrust), or neutral (constant thrust) burn profiles. Burn rate follows Saint Robert's law r = a*P^n, where the pressure exponent n (0.2-0.5) and the pre-exponential a are set by propellant formulation and binder plasticizer content.",
  "early_win": false,
